#: src/features/Landing/LandingPage.tsx:155
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"During conversations, FluencyPal keeps track of the mistakes you make. "
"Based on these patterns, it generates personalized language rules designed "
"specifically for your weak areas. You can then practice each rule "
"separately: read a short explanation, see clear examples, and speak with "
"the AI while focusing only on that aspect of the language. This allows you "
"to systematically improve the exact grammar or expression patterns that "
"cause you the most difficulty, turning your mistakes into targeted speaking "
"practice."
msgstr ""
"Semasa perbualan, FluencyPal menjejak kesilapan yang anda lakukan. "
"Berdasarkan corak ini, ia menghasilkan peraturan bahasa peribadi yang "
"direka khas untuk kawasan lemah anda. Anda kemudian boleh berlatih setiap "
"peraturan secara berasingan: membaca penerangan ringkas, melihat contoh "
"yang jelas, dan bercakap dengan AI sambil memberi tumpuan hanya pada aspek "
"bahasa itu. Ini membolehkan anda memperbaiki secara sistematik tatabahasa "
"atau corak ungkapan tertentu yang menyebabkan anda paling sukar, mengubah "
"kesilapan anda menjadi latihan bercakap yang disasarkan."

#: src/features/Usage/HoursPaymentModal/FaqHours.tsx:17
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"Each time you use AI features (like conversation or Role Play), it consumes "
"a certain amount of computational power, which we measure in \"hours of AI "
"usage.\" This allows us to fairly allocate resources based on your activity "
"level. I call it \"AI hours\" because it`s approximate time of which you "
"will consume the AI if you will use it continuously."
msgstr ""
"Setiap kali anda menggunakan ciri AI (seperti perbualan atau Main Peranan), "
"ia menggunakan sejumlah kuasa pengiraan tertentu, yang kami ukur dalam "
"\"jam penggunaan AI.\" Ini membolehkan kami memperuntukkan sumber dengan "
"adil berdasarkan tahap aktiviti anda. Saya menyebutnya \"jam AI\" kerana ia "
"adalah anggaran masa yang akan anda gunakan AI jika anda menggunakannya "
"secara berterusan."

